{"id":"u-a263984c-2c7a-4978-a30e-051cc479ff3e","src":"community","title":"Upper/Lower 4-Day Hypotrophy","author":"Kristoffer Astono","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/8LHh5K-hypotrophy","desc":"Unlock your muscle-building potential with the 12-week Hypotrophy program, designed for intermediate to advanced lifters. This 4-day split focuses on hypertrophy, maximizing muscle growth through targeted exercises and progressive overload. Utilizing a full gym setup, you'll engage in a variety of compound and isolation movements to sculpt your physique and enhance strength. Get ready to push your limits and transform your body with a structured approach that delivers results!\n\nWORKOUT INSTRUCTIONS:\n\nWARMUP:\nThe first two sets are warmup sets. For the first set find a weight that is 50-60% of your working weight and do 10 reps. For the second set find a weight that is 60-70% of your working weight. Do 8 reps with that. \n\nRest between warmup sets is ~90 seconds.\n\nWORK SETS:\nWe use the double progression model in the program. That means you find a weight that you can do 5-6 reps with 2RIR. So your first set is to be done @ 2RIR. When you can do 8 reps in the first set with the 2RIR, you find a weight that takes you back to 5-6 reps with 2RIR. \n\nRest between worksets is ~3 min.\n\nWORKING SETS:\n\nOn both upper and lower days there is 2 working sets. The first set is to be done at 2RIR. On the second set you do the same load, and match the reps you did on the first set. The RIR on the second set dosen't matter, but you should NOT go to failure. \n\nExample: \n\n1st set: 50 kg, 7 reps, 2 RIR.\n2nd set: 50 kg, 7 reps, 1 RIR.\n\nARMS HAVE 3 WORKING SETS. On the third set (backoff set) you reduce the load by around 10%, and do the same number of reps. \n\nExample: \n\n1st set: 50 kg, 7 reps, 2 RIR.\n2nd set: 50 kg, 7 reps, 1 RIR.\n3rd set: 45 kg,7 reps, 1RIR.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":1,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-03-14T14:49:38.934Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Upper A","Lower A","Upper B","Lower B"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6},{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Wide Grip Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6},{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6},{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Supported T-bar Row","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6},{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6},{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Leg Press (45 Degrees)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6},{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6},{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6},{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6},{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Calf Raise (Leg Press)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6},{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6},{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Shoulder Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6},{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown (Single Arm)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6},{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Chest Press","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6},{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Row (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6},{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6},{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Leg Press (45 Degrees)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":5},{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6},{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":5},{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6},{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":2}]},{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":5},{"lo":8,"hi"